  "notes": "West leads the ♦A against 4♥. West wins the first trick and continues diamonds. South has a critical decision to make. Should South play the ♦K or finesse at trick 2?\n\nThe easiest way to solve this problem is to think about what could go wrong with each play. If the ♦K is played and East ruffs, the contract will fail. East will return a spade and South will have no way of avoiding losing a trick in both spades and diamonds.\n\nIf the diamond finesse is taken at trick 2, nothing can go wrong. East may win the ♦Q and return a spade. North's diamond suit is now established to provide discards for South's spade and club losers once trump is drawn.\n\nIf East started with a singleton diamond, he will ruff at trick 2. Dummy's diamonds will again be established to take care of South's spade and club losers.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
